Set up Tailscale (private-cloud access path)?
  - Install tailscale from pkgs.tailscale.com (signed apt repository, noble): keyring /usr/share/keyrings/tailscale-archive-keyring.gpg, list /etc/apt/sources.list.d/tailscale.list
  - Run `tailscale up` and print its login URL for you to approve in a browser
  - Allow the harbor service account to manage serve entries: tailscale set --operator=harbor
  - Record the node name; Harbor only publishes apps you explicitly expose (tailscale serve, HTTPS with tailnet certificates)
  (approved with --yes)
