Set up the public proxy (Caddy, HTTPS with Let's Encrypt)?
  - Install caddy from dl.cloudsmith.io/public/caddy/stable (signed apt repository): keyring /usr/share/keyrings/caddy-stable-archive-keyring.gpg, list /etc/apt/sources.list.d/caddy-stable.list
  - Write a Harbor-owned JSON config /etc/caddy/harbor.json (admin API on 127.0.0.1:2019, no sites yet) and run caddy from it via a systemd drop-in (--resume keeps Harbor's changes across restarts)
  - Ports 80/443 stay closed until you expose an app; then DNS for each hostname must point at this host
  (approved with --yes)
